Iron pickaxe - A simple iron pickaxe used for mining.   (Quest Item)
Power Core - A crystal commonly used by the Iron Division Orcs to power their devices.   (Quest Item)
Moondrop Flower - The pale petals of this eerie smelling flower glisten in the moon light.   (Quest Item)
Scroll of Dispel Magic - This spell attempts to remove magic effects from a certain object.   (Quest Item)
Purple Root - This root is often used by alchemists and scribes to create pigment.   (Quest Item)
Bowl of Pigment - The mushy pigment reeks of an odd dirt-like smell.   (Quest Item)
Bowl of Fae Dust - The sparkly crystal powder feels warm to the touch.   (Quest Item)
Red Crystal - This small crystal seems to produce an everlasting source of heat.   (Quest Item)
Can of Enchanted Purple Ink - This ink is used by scribes to create spirit magic spell scrolls.   (Quest Item)
Toolkit - This box contains various tools used by the Fixers for maintenance work.   (Quest Item)
Iron Ingot - The heavy, cold bar is ready to be forged into a new shape.   (Quest Item)
Mithril Ingot - The oddly light bar gleams into the light.   (Quest Item)
Iron Ore - The rough ore needs to be smelt before it can be used.   (Quest Item)
Mithril Ore - This ore is highly sought after by blacksmiths for being able to create strong, lightweight items.   (Quest Item)
Empty Gear Mould - The mould contains the negative shape of a gear, and is ready to be filled with the proper metal.   (Quest Item)
Filled Gear Mould - The mould has been filled and the gear inside is hot and ready to be hammered on the anvil.   (Quest Item)
Mithril Gear - The gleaming gear looks as if it could support a large mechanism without the risk of breaking.   (Quest Item)
Book of Earth - This hefty manual contains numerous translations and incantations gathered along the ages by those who studied Earth Magic.   (Quest Item)
Shovel - A simple shovel with a sturdy blade and a sharp iron edge.   (Quest Item)
Wooden Plank - A well wrought wooden plank.   (Quest Item)
Vine - A resilient string of vine. The rock tied at the end should make it easy to throw and coil.   (Quest Item)
Cyan Crystal - The glowing crystal emits warmth and strange magnetic waves.   (Quest Item)
Keg of Dragonbrew - The volatile scent piercing through the wood feels like it could either bring someone back from the dead or kill them.   (Quest Item)
Hot Iron - A gleaming bar of iron, ready to be shaped on the anvil.   (Quest Item)
Iron Lever - A crudely crafted lever that can hook onto gate activating mechanisms.   (Quest Item)
Jar of Corrosive Acid - A large jar labelled with a menacing skull. Even the dark iron case seems to be slightly corroded by the acid inside.   (Quest Item)
Hunk of Flesh - A bloody hunk of flesh. You are not entirely sure of its' origin, but you would rather not know anyway.   (Quest Item)
Earth Figurine - A coarse ritual statuette depicting Earth.   (Quest Item)
Water Figurine - A cold ritual statuette depicting Water.   (Quest Item)
Air Figurine - A finely crafted ritual statuette depicting Air.   (Quest Item)
Fire Figurine - A dark ritual statuette depicting Fire.   (Quest Item)
Fire Fragment - A magical fragment instilled with the power of Fire.   (Quest Item)
Water Fragment - A magical fragment instilled with the power of Water.   (Quest Item)
Earth Fragment - A magical fragment instilled with the power of Earth.   (Quest Item)
Air Fragment - A magical fragment instilled with the power of Air.   (Quest Item)
Empty Potion Bottle - An iron-capped recipient that can safely store any liquid inside.   (Quest Item)
Mana Potion - This potent magic water is broadly used by mages to restore their energy.   (Quest Item)
Shovel - A plain shovel with a blade made from pig iron.   (Quest Item)
Sledgehammer - A massive hammer usually used to break rocks and walls.   (Quest Item)
Fire Oil - This hot bottle is filled with a bright volatile oil.   (Quest Item)
Ancient Dictionary - This tome translates words from an ancient human dialect into common demonic.   (Quest Item)
Spirit Gem - The round shaped gem feels chilling to the touch.   (Quest Item)
Body Gem - The square shaped gem weighs a lot more than it appears.   (Quest Item)
Mind Gem - The triangular shaped gem emits a numbing heat.   (Quest Item)
Soul Stone - The smooth surface of the oval stone pulsates with the power of a trapped soul.   (Quest Item)
Password Scroll - The oily paper is scribbled with random words.   (Quest Item)
Psi Crown - This weird device can presumably allow the wearer to pass through psionic fields unharmed.   (Quest Item)
Psishroom - The ethereal fungus emits strange vibrations.   (Quest Item)
Gold Coins - Although gold isn't of much value within the Iron Division, it is always welcome when trading with outsiders.   (Quest Item)
Giant Ruby - The flawlessly cut gem bears the heritage of the ancient minotaurs.   (Quest Item)
Dark Iron Ore - This ore is renown for yielding a metal imprevious to heat.   (Quest Item)
Intel Scroll - A paper containing confidential information about enemy positions and logistics. A tactician would most likely be interested in it.   (Quest Item)
Mysterious Recipe - The moldy parchment holds unknown alchemical secrets. A potion maker could probably understand them better.   (Quest Item)
Dwarven Lockbox - This finely crafted box feels emburdened with goods. A skilled locksmith might be able to unlock it.   (Quest Item)
Scroll Case - This ornate scroll case is sealed with fire magic runes. A knowledgeable mage could find it valuable.   (Quest Item)
Dwarven Mask - The fancy looking mask has a reinforced glass visor and a pair of odd tubes curving beneath.   (Quest Item)
Empty Dwarven Tank - The tank seems to be in a fairly good shape, but whatever was inside it is long gone now.   (Quest Item)
Dwarven Tank - The tank appears to be filled with something, although it weights less than expected.   (Quest Item)
Dwarven Suit - A dwarf-sized costume covered in waterproof grease. The oil has likely preserved the material through the ages.   (Quest Item)
Seed of Corruption - You have no clue what the strangely technologized jar is containing, but you're fairly sure it's staring at you.   (Quest Item)
Special Containment Jar - The jar was specifically designed to contain a Seed of Corruption.   (Quest Item)
Large Shell Warhead - The experimental warhead fuze looks ready to be inserted into a large caliber shell.   (Quest Item)
Large Shell Casing - An experimentally large caliber shell that can be filled with a sizable amount of explosive powder.   (Quest Item)
Large Shell - The experimentally large shell is ready to be loaded into a cannon.   (Quest Item)
Squirming Sand Nut - The hard shell fruit won't stop trying to squirm out of your hands. Maybe smashing it with a rock would make it stop.   (Quest Item)
Crimson Salt Rock - The tinted salt chunk is far too tough and dense to be edible.   (Quest Item)
Chaotic Device - The artifact may have once contained unholy powers, but now it looks like nothing more but a cold piece of metal.   (Quest Item)
Charged Chaotic Device - The artifact is charged with chaotic energy and feels highly unstable.   (Quest Item)
Pendant of True Sight - The silver medallion holds a magical eye capable of dispelling certain visual illusions.   (Quest Item)
Pendant of True Sight (Rebel) - The silver medallion holds a magical eye capable of dispelling visual illusions created by rebel cultists.   (Quest Item)
Pendant of True Sight (Servant) - The illusion-dispelling eye is charged with the memories of the succubus matron's gardner.   (Quest Item)
Winch Wheel - The crude wheel can be used to operate certain devices.   (Quest Item)
Bag of Yeast - The bag is filled with a vital ingredient for baking and brewing.   (Quest Item)
Orc Doll - The lovingly crafted rag doll resembles an Iron Division Lancer.   (Quest Item)
Primarch Avatar - The golden plate resonates with the voice of a demon primarch.   (Quest Item)
Soul Key Fragment - Tormented souls writhe inside this timeless prison.   (Quest Item)
Ritual Dagger - This golden dagger looks more fit for rituals rather than combat.   (Quest Item)
Piece of Perfumed Cloth - The fabric is imbued with the succubus matron's scent.   (Quest Item)
Lock of Hair - A strand of hair belonging to the Queen of Wrath.   (Quest Item)
Cursed Chalice - The demonic chalice feels a lot heavier than it looks.   (Quest Item)
Cursed Chalice - The cursed chalice seems to slowly replenish the liquid it contains. The blood inside bubbles restlessly.   (Quest Item)
Cursed Chalice - The cursed chalice seems to slowly replenish the liquid it contains. The oil inside is burning hot.   (Quest Item)
Scroll of Enchant Trinket - This spell can transfer the innate magical properties of an object to a valuable trinket.   (Quest Item)
Sacrificial Sword - The gaudy ruby blade seems more fit for taking life through ritual rather than combat.   (Quest Item)
Mithril Chisel - The perfectly balanced chisel could render even the hardest rock into a piece of art.   (Quest Item)
Cursed Chalice - The cursed chalice seems to slowly replenish the liquid it contains. The mana inside glows brightly.   (Quest Item)
Arcane Salts - Rare catalysts sought after by many alchemists, the arcane salts come in three colors: pink, green and cyan.   (Quest Item)
Hog Liver - The large hog liver could make for a hearty meal.   (Quest Item)
Deadly Poison - This poison is potent enough to kill someone within seconds, should they be tricked into ingesting it.   (Quest Item)
Sleeping Potion - The swirly fluid could put even the most watchful guardian to sleep.   (Quest Item)
Elixir of Life - The mere existence of this extremely potent substance is a myth. Rumors mention of a clan of orcs who discovered the Fountain of Life, centuries ago...   (Quest Item)
Elixir of Death - The pitch dark substance is rumored to not only kill the body, but the soul itself.   (Quest Item)
Anointed Phylactery - This sort of container is rumored to store the soul of someone who traded death for eternal lichdom.   (Quest Item)
Angel Feather - This feather is far too large to have belonged to a bird. It is uncertain whether it has magical properties or not.   (Quest Item)
Crimson Salt Statue - A masterfully crafted statue, portraying the champion of Valc as she strikes a fierce pose. Its staggering weight reminds of how dense and solid crimson salt is.   (Quest Item)
Pit Lord Head - The severed head of an arrogant pit lord who put his trust in the wrong person.   (Quest Item)
Depleted Armor Amulet - The amulet is completely lifeless, its wearer having been brutally assaulted and overwhelmed.   (Quest Item)
Mortar of Earth Pigment - This crystal-infused pigment is used by scribes to create earth magic spell scrolls.   (Quest Item)
Bowl of Scribe Embers - The mix of enchanted embers is used by scribes to create fire magic spell scrolls.   (Quest Item)
Iron-Bound Tome - This chained tome contains schematics for many outlawed weapons and artifacts. A blacksmith would find it invaluable.   (Quest Item)
Vial of Healing - This vial restores 10 hit points upon drinking.
Fixer's Goggles - While activated, these goggles will help you see through darkness with ease. Lasts until out of charge.
Potion of Stoneskin - Drinking this potion will turn your skin into stone scales, greatly increasing your physical, blast and nature damage resistance. Lasts 45 seconds.
Time Shard - Upon shattering this crystal, the user breaks the flow of time surrounding them, freezing most of the projectiles and creatures in their vicinity. Lasts about 10 seconds.
Scroll of Wizard's Eye - This spell will magically chart the surroundings, revealing them on the caster's map, also tracking the position of monsters and items.
Elemental Ring - This enchanted ring will greatly protect the wearer against elemental and magic damage, and give them underwater breath. Lasts 90 seconds.
Potion of Might - Drinking this will grant you ungodly strength but sap your dexterity. You gain HP regeneration and increased melee and throwing damage but your other ranged attacks will be weaker. Lasts 60 seconds.
Potion of Haste - Drinking this potion will instil you with a burst of magic that increases attack speed. Lasts 30 seconds.
Sentry Gun - One of the most advanced weaponry of the Iron Division, the Sentry Gun can be deployed to provide cover and security within a certain area.
Amulet of Shadows - Wearing this dark crystal will turn you into a blurry shadow, making you faster and harder to aim at. Lasts 75 seconds.
Choker of the Beast - Wearing this collar will shroud you in a fearsome vampiric aura, forcing most enemies to flee and giving your attacks the ability to drain life. Lasts 30 seconds.
Bracer of the Revenant - Equipping this artifact will enchant your Axe to strike with the frigid power of Ice. Lasts 120 seconds.
Mystery Potion - A strange looking layered potion. You have no clue what effect it would have upon drinking.
Scroll of Inferno - This highly unstable spell will cause enemies within the reach of the caster to burst into explosive carnage.
Diving Suit - This air-tight suit allows the wearer to stay underwater for extended periods of time, while also protecting them against certain hazards. Lasts until out of charge.
Charged Psi Crown - The artifact is charged and ready to protect the wearer against a good portion of mind damage. Lasts until out of charge.
Boots of Journey - When equipped, this pair of old, inconspicuous boots will lighten the wearer's legs and increase movement speed. Lasts until unequipped
Ring of the Red Monk - When equipped, this ring will greatly increase unarmed damage, as well as bestow the user's fists with the legendary power of the Red Monks. Lasts until unequipped.
Scroll of Magma Ball - This spell will hurl a ball of magma that explodes on impact.
Nourish - This spell will fill the caster's body with nurturing energies, slowly regenerating their wounds. Lasts 60 seconds.
Journal - This handful of greasy, coarse papers bound by shaky iron hoops is more than enough to track your tasks on the battlefield.
Enchanted Purple Ink Recipe - Reading this scroll could offer some insight on how to brew enchanted purple ink.
Great Forge Instructions - Reading this scroll could offer some insight on how to operate the Great Forge's equipment.
Damp Note - Reading this note could offer some insight on what it is supposed to represent.
Mansion Sketch - Reading this sketch could offer some important information about the mansion grounds.
Ancient City Map - The ancient map inside the breached case seems to have been dmaged by the elements and passage of time.
